    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>Weekly Assignments: Weekly Assignment x4 = 10% each, Field trip report = 15%</div>\n\n<div>Final Project: Presentation: 15%, Report: 30%</div>\n",
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "Students must attend class in either Week 1 or Week 2 to participate in essential course arrangements, including group formation, scheduling, and course management. Failure to do so will result in being unable to complete the course.\n\nAdditionally:\n1. Punctuality matters. Arriving late or leaving early may result in being marked absent.\n2. Use respectful language. Inappropriate language will lead to immediate dismissal from the class.\n3. Respect and integrity. Treat all classmates and instructors with respect. Discrimination, harassment, or dishonesty will be addressed according to university policies.\n4. Collaborate and support peers. Group work is encouraged, and helping others can enhance everyone’s learning experience.\n5. Take responsibility for missed work. If you miss a class, it’s your responsibility to catch up on the material.\n6. Collaborative Effort in Group Work: All members of a group are expected to contribute equally to the final project. Ensure clear communication, share responsibilities, and support one another. If any group member consistently fails to contribute, the issue should be reported to the instructor immediately, and individual grades may be adjusted accordingly\n7. Use of AI Tools: ChatGPT and other AI tools may be used as supplementary resources. However, assignments must reflect the student's own understanding and effort. If a student cannot explain or elaborate on the content of their work, the assignment will receive a zero score.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "I hope that all students can complete various learning tasks according to the teaching progress, participate actively in all learning activities, and submit assignments on time. Completing these tasks will help you meet the learning objectives of this course and achieve the grades you deserve. If you encounter any difficulties during the semester, please don't hesitate to make use of my office hours, or schedule a separate appointment so we can work together to find solutions. Additionally, I encourage you to collaborate with your peers on the final project, as group study and shared insights can greatly enhance your understanding and performance.",
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Learning should be grounded in integrity. Any student who submits work that is not their own will be considered dishonest. Cheating or plagiarism in assignments or reports will result in a score of zero. You are allowed to quote or reference the words or ideas of others from publications, websites, or other sources, as long as you properly cite them. Originality is essential; any plagiarized work will receive a &quot;0&quot; or a &quot;fail&quot; grade. Repeat offenses will be handled according to the student conduct policies of Feng Chia University.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
